file: appstyle.cpp
suite: ui
test: paletteCoversBothThemes
why: a colour defined in one palette and not the other does not report a miss
     -- Utility::mAppColors is seeded with a default for most names, so
     getAppQColor finds the other theme's value and logs nothing. This was
     found by trying to write a light-tier mutation for
     noMissingIconsOrColours and watching it not be caught
--- from
        Utility::setAppQColor("disabledText", QColor(110,110,110));
--- to

